---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Portrait from '../components/Portrait.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, AUTHOR_SAME_AS, KNOWS_ABOUT, SITE } from '../lib/site.mjs';
const pub = SITE.publisher;
---

<Base
	title="About Emin Mahrt | emin.de"
	description="Emin Mahrt is a journalist, the publisher of proud magazine, and builds Bitcoin self-custody and agent-payment infrastructure. This is where he writes in full."
	path="/about"
	markdownPath="/about/index.md"
>
	<div class="about-top">
		<div>
			<p class="kicker">{pub.role.en}</p>
			<h1>About</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				I'm {AUTHOR_NAME}, a product engineer and founder from Berlin, the publisher of {pub.publication.name}, and I'm building
				nuri.com. This site is where all of it gets written down properly, at a length that fits the subject.
			</p>
		</div>
		<Portrait name={AUTHOR_NAME} eager />
	</div>

	<h2>Since 1999</h2>
	<p>
		German-Turkish IT guy since 1999, Berlin. I'm a product engineer and founder, shipping software since 1999. My work spans
		consumer apps, ad-tech, blockchain infrastructure and fintech.
	</p>
	<p>
		In Berlin, I founded <a href={pub.publication.url}>{pub.publication.name}</a>, an independent socio-political publication
		recognized by the <a href="https://www.dfjv.de">DFJV</a> and archived in the
		<a href="https://d-nb.info/992028108">German National Library</a>. I co-founded <a href="https://abend.net">abend.net</a>,
		an ML-driven ad optimization platform, and <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NwmK8omRuok">abend.com</a>, a Facebook
		Events discovery app, together serving thousands of paying clients monthly.
	</p>
	<p>
		After passing the technical engineering interview from Facebook I decided to pass on that and became COO and CPO of the
		newly founded <a href="https://aeternity.com">æternity Blockchain</a> in 2017. I led product and operations, scaled the
		team to over 100 people, and contributed to Liechtenstein's Blockchain Act. In 2022 I served as Chief Product Officer at
		<a href="https://www.bsdex.com">Börse Stuttgart Digital Exchange</a>, leading product for one of Europe's first regulated
		crypto trading platforms.
	</p>
	<p>
		I've been in Bitcoin since 2012: early mining, visiting
		<a href="https://www.coindesk.com/tech/2020/10/19/closing-time-for-bitcoins-iconic-room-77-and-thats-ok-says-owner">Room 77</a>,
		and contributing to different open source projects.
	</p>
	<p>
		Now I'm building <a href="https://nuri.com">nuri.com</a>. We acquired the Nuri brand after its insolvency, rebuilt the product
		from scratch, and launched the first and only passkey-derived and owned self-custodial Bitcoin wallet with non-custodial
		Visa card and integrated banking, live on iOS and Android across Europe, expanding to 100+ countries with a stablecoin
		Visa/Mastercard, onchain Euro IBAN and USD ACH account.
	</p>

	<h2>Journalist and publisher</h2>
	<p>
		The core rule of this site comes from {pub.publication.name}: <strong>free speech. Nothing here is censored. AI help is
		labelled, the words are mine.</strong> The details are on the <a href="/principles">principles page</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		<a href="mailto:emin@emin.de">emin@emin.de</a> · <a href="https://x.com/em" rel="me noopener">X</a> ·
		<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/bitcoinlightning/" rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a> ·
		<a href="https://signal.me/#eu/_JNAHwkQcIQ4HU8MVuWrO_WTnBcEzq8OND-0DT5VF6Xr_Lq6jmVF4rH0sM4Oq671" rel="noopener">Signal</a>
	</p>

	<h2>What I work on</h2>
	<p>
		Wallets where the company holding the keys is not a dependency: passkeys carrying their own secret through the
		WebAuthn PRF extension, MuSig2 co-signing that decays to a single key on a Bitcoin timelock, and the recovery
		tooling that has to work when the provider is gone.
	</p>
	<p>
		Alongside that, the agent side: x402 payments so software can pay for access without a signup flow, MCP servers
		so a model can call a system instead of scraping it, and the unglamorous work of making a website legible to
		both a search crawler and an agent.
	</p>

	<h2>What I write about here</h2>
	<ul>
		{KNOWS_ABOUT.map((topic) => <li>{topic}</li>)}
	</ul>

	<h2>How these articles get written</h2>
	<p>
		Long-form, one subject per piece, and only about things I actually built or measured. Every article opens with a
		TL;DR so you can leave early, carries a standalone takeaway per section, and ends with its real sources. If a
		number is in here, it came from a run I can point at.
	</p>
	<p>
		Each article is also published as clean Markdown at its own URL, included in a public JSON API, and exposed
		through an MCP server. That is deliberate: the writing should be as easy for a model to quote correctly as it is
		for a person to read.
	</p>

	<h2>Who else writes here</h2>
	<p>
		Some short posts may come from the <a href="/author/ai-desk">AI desk</a>: an openly named AI writing desk, not a person.
		Its posts carry the AI-written badge on the page, in the Markdown mirror and in the structured data.
		It has no invented biography and no photo.
	</p>

	<h2>Elsewhere</h2>
	<ul>
		{AUTHOR_SAME_AS.map((url) => <li><a href={url} rel="me noopener">{url.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '')}</a></li>)}
	</ul>

	<p><a href="/contact">Contact</a> if you are working on something adjacent.</p>
</Base>
